      "where": "foreign-policy.concepts / intl-orgs.general",
      "detail": "Q16 (ECOWAS, OAU, AU and other bodies are examples of what) is cited as tested under foreign-policy.concepts, but that subtopic's own sorting rule sends what an international organisation is and its types to intl-orgs.general, and intl-orgs.general's own sorting rule claims a question spanning several named organisations. The two covers lines point the same content at each other. The border needs a rule that survives its own citations, for example: a question naming several organisations to illustrate the category international organisation goes to intl-orgs.general regardless of whether the stem also uses the phrase foreign policy or international relations."
